/* ZCODE — 204 never_remote leaves (zcode.workspace.source.bundle.fetch is
 * owner_capability above).
 *
 * The C23 Commons branch builds, seals, installs, publishes, reproduces and
 * pays for packages. Its commands execute fetched source under the bounded
 * build lifecycle and publish signed artifacts. AGENTS.md is explicit that
 * fetching and storing are separate from building and testing, and that both
 * are separate from installing, linking, executing and deploying — each step
 * being a LOCAL acceptance a remote caller cannot perform on the operator's
 * behalf. A remote `zcode ... build` would collapse that ladder into one wire
 * call.
 *
 * Its reads are not promoted either, and the reason is the read_only test
 * rather than any specific danger: rewards, leaderboards, patronage, badges,
 * impact shares, corpus and moderation state answer "what is happening in the
 * commons", not "what is this machine doing". Several read-shaped leaves here
 * also carry mutating verbs (.commit, .capture, .rebuild, .begin, .cancel),
 * which is a second reason not to promote the branch on macro shape alone.
 *
 * Only the fetch is promoted, because converging a machine you own to a named
 * source root is the one Commons operation the fleet dev loop needs and the
 * only one whose acceptance is a hash the caller already knows. */
REMOTE_COMMAND_CLASS("zcode.workspace.source.capture", REMOTE_CLASS_NEVER, "")
REMOTE_COMMAND_CLASS("zcode.workspace.source.bundle.create", REMOTE_CLASS_NEVER, "")
